WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.375
Now the rule that beats almost every other rule: overtaking.

2
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:07.700
Rule thirteen opens with a strong phrase.

3
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:17.000
Notwithstanding anything in Rules four through eighteen, any vessel overtaking any other shall keep out of the way of the vessel being overtaken.

4
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.875
Any vessel.

5
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:20.625
Any other.

6
00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:23.100
So what counts as overtaking?

7
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.175
Look at the diagram.

8
00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:32.950
You’re overtaking when you come up on another vessel from a direction more than twenty-two and a half degrees abaft her beam.

9
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.725
That’s the shaded zone behind her.

10
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:39.350
At night, there’s an easy way to know.

11
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.550
From that zone, you can see only her sternlight, and neither of her sidelights.

12
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.000
One white light ahead of you, and you’re closing on it?

13
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.900
You’re overtaking, and you keep clear.

14
00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:55.950
And because this rule overrides the others, the kind of boat doesn’t matter.

15
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.400
A sailboat overtaking a powerboat keeps clear.

16
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:03.150
A fishing vessel overtaking anyone keeps clear.
